    "title": "College Basketball Roundup: Purdue, Illinois, Stanford, Texas Tech, Arkansas, and Mississippi Secure Wins",
    "text": "• Purdue defeated Iowa 79-72.\n• Braden Smith scored all 16 of his points in the second half.\n• Smith tied the Big Ten record for assists in conference play.\n• Trey Kaufman-Renn added 12 points for Purdue.\n• Bennett Stirtz led Iowa with 19 points.\n• Illinois beat Northwestern 79-68.\n• Keaton Wagler scored 22 points for Illinois.\n• Jayden Reid led Northwestern with 28 points.\n• Stanford defeated North Carolina 95-90.\n• Ebuka Okorie had 36 points and 9 assists for Stanford.\n• Jeremy Dent-Smith and Ryan Agarwal each scored 20 points for Stanford.\n• JT Toppin had 31 points and 13 rebounds for Texas Tech, who beat Utah 88-74.\n• Christian Anderson had 26 points and 10 assists for Texas Tech.\n• Darius Acuff Jr. had 18 points and 13 assists as Arkansas routed South Carolina 108-74.\n• Meleek Thomas led Arkansas with 21 points.\n• Mississippi defeated Georgia 97-95 in overtime.\n• Patton Pinkins scored the winning basket for Mississippi with 1 second remaining in overtime.\n• Jeremiah Wilkinson scored 32 points for Georgia.",
